gpui_ios sends no key events: a hardware keyboard's ⌘B, arrows, Tab and Esc never reached GPUI's actions, the soft keyboard's Return arrived as insertText("\n") and Delete at the start of the editable range was dropped, so an editor whose input handler covers one block could neither split nor merge blocks. pressesBegan now turns keys GPUI binds (anything with ⌘ or ⌃, and the named keys) into KeyDown/KeyUp, leaving plain typing and unhandled keys to UIKit and composition to the IME; Return outside composition and Delete at the range start become the enter and backspace keys. Needs objc2-ui-kit's UIKey, UIKeyConstants, UIPress and UIPressesEvent features.

